# What publish.sh leaves out of the public tree (public spec §14, ADR 0007): one git glob
# pathspec a line, matched against the private commit's tracked files; `#` starts a comment.
# Everything else that is tracked is published: source, tests, docs, .scratch, prototypes,
# licences, and the rest of refs/ (our analysis scripts, the opening book, API specifications).

# The third-party papers and web pages saved under refs/: refs/README.md cites them by link.
refs/**/*.pdf
refs/**/*.html

